1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,850
Lionel Messi’s first Barcelona contract… was written on a paper napkin.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:09,650
As a boy in Rosario, Argentina, he was always the smallest player on the pitch.

3
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:14,050
At around 11, doctors found his body wasn’t making enough growth hormone.

4
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:19,000
The treatment meant injections, night after night… reportedly about $1,000 a month.

5
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:22,400
At 13, he flew to Barcelona for a trial.

6
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:25,750
The coaches were impressed… but the club kept stalling.

7
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,200
His family threatened to take him home.

8
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:31,700
So on December 14, 2000, director Carles Rexach…

9
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:36,950
…grabbed the nearest piece of paper… a napkin… and wrote down a promise to sign him.

10
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,900
Barcelona paid for his treatment.

11
00:00:38,950 --> 00:00:44,550
That small boy went on to win 8 Ballon d’Or awards… and the World Cup.

12
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:50,300
And the napkin? In 2024, it sold at auction for nearly a million dollars.

13
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:55,700
Best signing ever… or can you name a better one?
